80 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (Low-code development platforms \(LCDPs\) allow individuals to design, build, and deploy applications using visual interfaces, pre-built components, and configuration rather than hand-written code. No-code platforms extend this idea further, removing the need for any coding at all. Together, these platforms have become central to how organizations respond to a persistent shortage of professional software developers, growing backlogs of internal IT )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
81 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H2
/P 61 0 R
/T (1. Executive Summary )
/E (1. Executive Summary )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
82 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (Low-code development has moved from a niche productivity tool to a foundational layer of enterprise software delivery. Analyst estimates converge on the same broad conclusion: by 2026, a substantial majority of new enterprise applications are being built with low-code or no-code technologies, with market forecasts placing the global low-code platform market in the range of roughly USD 40 to 49 billion in 2026, on a trajectory toward several hundred billion dollars by the mid-2030s. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
83 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (This report focuses on the leading low-code and no-code platforms that organizations are actually choosing between in 2026. It profiles ten of the most widely evaluated platforms side by side, covering what each is best known for, its typical buyer, and its general pricing posture, closing with a master comparison table intended as a quick-reference decision aid. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
84 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 61 0 R
/E (The report also addresses the risks that accompany rapid low-code and AI-agent adoption, including new categories of shadow IT and shadow AI, and closes with practical takeaways for decision-makers choosing or renewing a low- code strategy. )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
